      "text": "Nephi1 writes things pleasing unto God, not pleasing unto world, 1 Ne. 6:5 (2 Ne. 5:32). if Nephites are pleased with things of God, they will be pleased with engravings of Nephi1, 2 Ne. 5:32. tenderness and chasteness of feelings are pleasing unto God, Jacob 2:7. Jacob2 supposes people come to hear pleasing word of God, Jacob 2:8. meet before pleasing bar of God, Jacob 6:13 (Moro. 10:34). it pleased the Lord to bruise him, Mosiah 14:10 (Isa. 53:10). Korihor taught devil’s words because they were pleasing to carnal mind, Alma 30:53. behold my Beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased, 3 Ne. 11:7 (Matt. 3:17).",
